    "summary": "A woman&#039;s fez / hat / skull-cap.  Upper part of sides (7.5 cms deep) and round, flat top completely covered with embroidery using silver wire.  A sixteen-petalled blossom in the centre with four stylized leaves radiating outwards.  Between each leaf a six-petalled flower.  Sides have big zigzag pattern with an alternating small flower and leaf in each niche.  &#039;Ground&#039; is a basket-weave style stitch.  Crimson red felt (6 cms) stitched (white cotton yarn) to lower section of fez.  Fez stiffened with paper on sides and cardboard at top.  Small holes in felt; faded near base.",
